messages.content:
# Fix: Workspace data not reaching `AppWindow` / `Tab`

## Direct recommendation

The workspace object (name, path, metadata) is being **dropped at the payload boundary**: `ui.openWorkspace` wraps it under `params`, `navigation.workspaces.open` only forwards `{ key, name }`, and neither `Tab` nor `AppWindow` knows how to read the workspace when it *does* arrive. Pass the full workspace object under a `workspace` key (mirroring the `chat` convention) and teach `Tab` + `AppWindow` to read `params.workspace`.

## Specifications

| Concern | Current behavior | Fixed behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `navigation.workspaces.open` payload | `{ workspace: { key, name } }` — drops path & metadata | `{ workspace: <full object> }` (accepts object *or* legacy id/name) |
| `ui.openWorkspace` payload | `{ params: workspace }` — wrong key, workspace lost | `{ workspace }` — matches the app's `desktopParams` contract |
| `Tab` title source | `chat?.name ‖ app?.title ‖ tabName` (clueless about workspaces) | `chat?.name ‖ workspace?.name ‖ app?.title ‖ app?.name ‖ tabName` |
| `AppWindow` target | `app ‖ params.app ‖ params.app` | `app ‖ params.workspace ‖ params.app ‖ params.app` |

## Changes

### 1. `src/router/navigate.js` — forward the whole workspace

```js js src/router/navigate.js

    workspaces: {
      list() {
        openApp('workspaces')
      },

      open(workspaceOrId, workspaceName) {
        // Accept either a full workspace object (preferred: carries name,
        // path and any other metadata) or a legacy (id, name) pair.
        const workspace = (workspaceOrId && typeof workspaceOrId === 'object')
          ? workspaceOrId
          : { key: workspaceOrId, name: workspaceName }

        if (!workspace?.key) {
          console.warn('[Navigation] workspaces.open: invalid workspace', workspaceOrId)
          return
        }

        const name = workspace.name || `workspace-${workspace.key}`

        // Check if currently in chat view
        if ($navigation.isChatView) {
          const chatId = $navigation.getChatId()
          const chatName = $navigation.getChatName()

          if (chatId) {
            $navigation.chats.openWithWorkspace(chatId, chatName, workspace.key, name)
            return
          }
        }

        // Forward the full workspace under the `workspace` key (same
        // convention as `chat`) so name/path reach the panel params.
        openApp('workspace', { workspace })
      }
    },
```

### 2. `src/store/ui.js` — fix the payload key

```js js src/store/ui.js

    openWorkspace(_, workspace) {
      if (!workspace || !workspace.key) {
        console.warn('[UI] openWorkspace: invalid workspace', workspace)
        return
      }
      // Forward the whole workspace under the `workspace` key so the app's
      // desktopParams can lift name/path into the panel params.
      $storex.ui.openApp({ appKey: 'workspace', payload: { workspace } })
    },
```

### 3. `src/components/desktop/Tab.vue` — read the workspace for its label

```vue vue src/components/desktop/Tab.vue
<script setup>
import AppIcon from '../apps/AppIcon.vue'
</script>
<template>
  <div
    class="codx-tab flex gap-1 items-center justify-between px-1 py-0.5 border rounded-xl w-40 text-md"
    :draggable="!!chat"
    :class="{ 'cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing': !!chat }"
    @dragstart="onDragStart"
  >
    <div class="w-4/5 flex gap-1 items-center truncate overflow-hidden">
      <!-- Pass loading state to AppIcon so it shows the ring inside the icon area -->
      <AppIcon :app="app || workspace" :loading="isUpdating" />
      <div class="grow truncate overflow-hidden">{{ tabName }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="click hover:text-warning shrink-0 mr-2" @click="onClose">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark fa-sm"></i>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>
<script>

export default {
  props: ['params'],
  data() {
    return {
      project: null,
    }
  },
  async created() {
    this.project = this.$projects.allProjectsById[this.projectId]
  },
  computed: {
    chat() {
      const chatId = this.params?.params?.chat?.id
      return this.$storex.chats.chats[chatId]
    },
    // Workspace panels carry the raw workspace (name, path, …) in params
    workspace() {
      return this.params?.params?.workspace
    },
    app() {
      return this.params?.params?.app
    },
    tabName() {
      return this.chat?.name ||
        this.workspace?.name ||
        this.workspace?.title ||
        this.app?.title ||
        this.app?.name ||
        this.params?.params?.tabName
    },
    api() {
      return this.params.api
    },
    containerApi() {
      return this.params.containerApi
    },
    panel() {
      return this.api.panel
    },
    projectId() {
      return this.params.params.project_id
    },
    isUpdating() {
      return this.$storex.chats.isChatUpdating(this.chat?.id)
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onDragStart(event) {
      // Only register a sprint task id when the tab is backed by a chat
      if (!this.chat) return
      event.dataTransfer.setData('sprintTaskId', this.chat.id)
      event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move'
    },
    onClose() {
      this.containerApi.removePanel(this.panel)
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### 4. `src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue` — resolve the workspace as the window target

```vue vue src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue
<script setup>
import Iframe from '../Iframe.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="w-full h-full" :class="loaded ? '' : 'opacity-0'">
    <Iframe
      ref="iframe"
      class="w-full h-full"
      :key="theApp.path"
      :url="currentUrl"
      @loaded="onLoaded"
      @navigated="onNavigated"
    />
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: "AppWindow",
  props: ['app', 'params'],
  data() {
    return {
      loaded: false,
      currentUrl: null
    }
  },
  created() {
    const app = this.theApp
    // Restore last navigated URL from params or fall back to app path
    this.currentUrl = this.params?.params?.lastUrl || app?.path
    this.loaded = app?.is_vnc
  },
  computed: {
    theApp() {
      // Prefer the explicit prop, then the workspace payload (name + path +
      // metadata), then the app definition and the legacy params slot.
      return this.app ||
        this.params?.params?.workspace ||
        this.params?.params?.app ||
        this.params?.app
    },
    tabId() {
      return this.theApp?.tabId
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onLoaded() {
      this.loaded = true
      // Read the actual current URL and title from the iframe after load
      this.readIframeUrl()
      this.$emit('loaded')
    },
    // Read URL and title directly from iframe contentWindow after navigation
    readIframeUrl() {
      try {
        const iframeEl = this.$refs.iframe?.$el || this.$refs.iframe
        const contentWindow = iframeEl?.contentWindow
        const url = contentWindow?.location?.href
        const title = contentWindow?.document?.title
        if (url && url !== 'about:blank') {
          this.onNavigated(url, title)
        }
      } catch (e) {
        // Cross-origin access blocked, silently ignore
      }
    },
    // Track url changes and persist them in the app params via store
    onNavigated(url, title) {
      if (!url || url === this.currentUrl) return
      this.currentUrl = url
      this.persistUrl(url, title)
    },
    // Persist current URL and page title so layout restore can recover them
    persistUrl(url, title) {
      if (!this.tabId) return
      const params = { lastUrl: url }
      // Only store title if it's a non-empty valid string
      if (title && title.trim()) {
        params.title = title.trim()
      }
      this.$storex.ui.updateAppParams({
        tabId: this.tabId,
        params
      })
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Anti-patterns avoided

- ❌ **Mismatched payload keys between entry points** — `ui.openApp` used `params` while `navigation.openApp` uses semantic keys like `chat`/`workspace`. That single inconsistency silently discarded every field except what `desktopParams` could still find.
- ❌ **Reading only `params.app` for metadata** — both `Tab` and `AppWindow` assumed every panel is "app-shaped", so workspace-shaped params were invisible.
- ❌ **Building payloads by hand at each call site** — prefer passing the domain object (the workspace) intact and letting `desktopParams` decide the shape.

## Accessibility checklist

- Tab label now resolves to a real string for workspaces (no empty/garbled label → better screen-reader output).
- No change to keyboard/close-button semantics; `@click` handler and drag behavior untouched.
- Icons still receive an app-like object (`app || workspace`), preserving the visual cue for low-vision users.

## Implementation steps

1. Update `navigation.workspaces.open` to forward the full workspace under `{ workspace }` (accepts legacy id/name too).
2. Update `ui.openWorkspace` to pass `{ workspace }` instead of `{ params: workspace }`.
3. Add the `workspace` computed + label fallback in `Tab.vue`.
4. Add the `workspace` fallback to `theApp` in `AppWindow.vue`.
5. Verify: open a workspace → the tab shows the workspace **name** and the iframe loads the workspace **path**; confirm chat tabs still show chat names (chat takes priority in `tabName`).

