## Change summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/router/navigate.js` | `workspaces.open` accepts a **full workspace object** (or legacy id/name) and forwards it entire under `{ workspace }` |
| `src/store/ui.js` | `openWorkspace` payload changed from `{ params: workspace }` → `{ workspace }` |
| `src/components/desktop/Tab.vue` | New `workspace` computed; `tabName` falls back to `workspace.name/title`; icon switches on `app ‖ workspace` |
| `src/components/windowManager/AppWindow.vue` | `theApp` resolves `params.workspace` so its `path`/metadata reach the iframe |

## Anti-patterns avoided

- ❌ **Mismatched payload keys** – `ui.openApp` reads semantic keys (`chat`, `workspace`); the store was wrapping the workspace under `params`, which `desktopParams` ignores.
- ❌ **Hand-built trimmed payloads** – always forward the domain object intact so `path`, `icon`, and future fields survive.
- ❌ **App-only assumptions** – panels can be app- *or* workspace-shaped; both `Tab` and `AppWindow` now look for the workspace branch.

## Accessibility checklist

- Tab label now resolves to a real string for workspaces (no empty/garbled label → correct screen-reader output).
- Icon change keeps a visible affordance without relying on color alone.
- No change to drag/close semantics or keyboard reachability.

## Implementation steps

1. Update `navigation.workspaces.open` to accept/forward the full workspace under `{ workspace }`.
2. Update `ui.openWorkspace` to pass `{ workspace }` instead of `{ params: workspace }`.
3. Add the `workspace` computed + label fallback in `Tab.vue`.
4. Add the `workspace` branch to `theApp` in `AppWindow.vue`.
5. Verify: open a workspace → **tab shows the workspace name**, and the **iframe loads the workspace path**; confirm chat tabs still prefer `chat.name`.

